Interview pattern to remember
The key optimization is:
Count nodes in a complete binary tree
              ↓
Find leftmost and rightmost heights
              ↓
         Are they equal?
           /       \
         Yes        No
          ↓          ↓
     Perfect tree   Recurse
          ↓          ↓
    2^(h+1) - 1   1 + left + right


Your code uses exactly this idea.
Remember these two facts:
1. Equal leftmost and rightmost heights mean the subtree is perfect for a complete-tree input.
2. A perfect subtree with height h measured in edges contains \(2^{h+1}-1\) nodes.
Those two properties are what reduce the running time from \(O(n)\) to \(O(\log^2 n)\).
